{"study_accession":"PRJNA1164135","secondary_study_accession":"SRP534156","title":"Systemic Lupus Erythematosus (SLE) samples for Juvenile Sjogrens Syndrome (JSS) Transcriptome Study","description":"To investigate the inflammatory signature and transcriptomical changes in CD14 positive monocytes, we have isolated and purified monocytes cells from whole blood. Bulk RNA-seq were conducted with an Illumina Novaseq 6000 (Illumina, San Diego, CA, USA), which generated paired-end (PE) reads of approximately 100 bp in size. According to the instruction of the NEBNext Ultra RNA Library Prep Kit (Illumina, San Diego, CA, USA), a sequential process of end-repair, poly-A addition, and adaptor ligation on both ends was carried out. A total of 43 samples involving 6 healthy control, 7 Sjogren Syndrome (SjS), 8 Systemic Lupus Erythematosus (SLE), 7 Juvenile Sjogren Syndrome (JSS), 9 Biopsy Test Positive (Bx+), and 6 Non-Juvenile Sjogren Syndrome (non-SjS), were collected and sequenced.","pubmed":"","geo_series":"","n_samples":8,"samples":[{"sample_accession":"SAMN43886063","study_accession":"PRJNA1164135","blood_class":"whole_blood","class_from":"sample","title":"Systemic Lupus Erythematosus (SLE)","description":"Systemic Lupus Erythematosus (SLE)","sex":"female","geo_sample":"","access":"open","dbgap":"","n_runs":1,"first_public":"2025-03-03","attributes":[["isolate","Whole blood"],["age","45"],["biomaterial_provider","Seunghee Cha, DDS, PhD"],["collection_date","2019"],["geo_loc_name","USA: Florida"],["sex","female"],["tissue","Whole blood"],["cell_subtype","Monocytes"],["cell_type","white blood cell"],["disease_stage","Systemic Lupus Erythematosus (SLE)"]],"runs":[{"run_accession":"SRR30767654","experiment_accession":"SRX26170004","library_layout":"PAIRED","library_selection":"cDNA_oligo_dT","instrument_model":"Illumina NovaSeq 6000","read_count":28770545,"base_count":5811650090,"first_public":"2025-03-03","experiment_title":"Illumina NovaSeq 6000 sequencing: Bulk RNA-seq of m